---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { SITE, AUTHOR, WAITLIST, ANALYTICS } from '../data/site.mjs'

const url = `${SITE.url}/privacy/`
const updated = '2026-08-31'
const fmt = new Date(updated).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' })

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'WebPage',
      '@id': `${url}#page`,
      url,
      name: `Privacy — ${SITE.name}`,
      dateModified: updated,
      isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#website` },
      publisher: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` },
    },
  ],
}
---
<Base
  title={`Privacy — ${SITE.name}`}
  description="What Suvi collects, who processes it, how long it is kept, and how to have it deleted. Plain language, no boilerplate."
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />

  <article class="pv shell">
    <nav class="pv__crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> <span>Privacy</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="pv__h1">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="pv__meta">Last updated {fmt}</p>

    <div class="pv__body">
      <p class="pv__lede">
        This page describes what this website collects. Suvi the product has not
        shipped yet, so nothing here covers a running app or a child's device —
        when that exists it will get its own policy, and we will say so before
        anything changes.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The only thing we ask you for is an email address, plus three optional questions.</li>
        <li>Analytics cookies are not set unless you press Accept.</li>
        <li>We do not sell anything to anyone, and we run no advertising.</li>
        <li>No child uses this website. It is written for parents.</li>
        <li>Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> and we will delete your data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we collect, and when</h2>

      <h3>If you join the waitlist</h3>
      <p>
        The form asks for an email address. When you submit it, the following is
        sent to our waitlist provider:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your email address.</strong></li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your email address a second time, in the name field.</strong> Our
          provider requires a first and last name. Rather than invent a plausible
          name from your address, we put the address itself in the first-name field
          and a dash in the last-name field, so nothing in our records is a guess
          about who you are.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The address of the page you signed up from</strong>, so we know
          which article brought you.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>If you answer the three questions</h3>
      <p>
        After signing up you are shown three optional questions. Skipping them is
        a normal outcome and costs you nothing. If you answer, we store what you
        typed alongside your email:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your child's age, as a band rather than a birthday.</li>
        <li>Which apps or sites you already use.</li>
        <li>Where you want help.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The age band is information about a child, given by a parent. We ask for a
        band and not a date of birth precisely so it cannot identify anyone, and
        we do not ask for a child's name, school, photograph or anything else
        about them. If you would rather we held nothing about your child at all,
        skip that question — the waitlist works exactly the same.
      </p>

      <h3>If you accept analytics</h3>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics 4 to see which pages are read and which are
        ignored. Every storage category starts <em>denied</em>, worldwide and not
        only in Europe, and nothing is stored until you press Accept. If you press
        Decline, or ignore the banner, no analytics cookie is set.
      </p>
      <p>
        With consent, Google Analytics records the pages you visit, roughly where
        you are from a truncated IP address, your device and browser, and where
        you arrived from. We also record that a waitlist signup happened and
        whether the questions were answered — the count, never the answers
        themselves.
      </p>
      <p>
        Advertising consent is never requested and never granted. Suvi runs no
        advertising and we have no interest in building an advertising profile of
        you.
      </p>

      <h2>Things that happen without asking you</h2>
      <p>
        Two of these are unavoidable in a browser and one is a choice we have not
        yet fixed. Naming them is more useful than pretending they do not exist.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is served by GitHub Pages. Like any
          web server, GitHub receives your IP address in order to send you the
          page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fonts.</strong> The page loads its typefaces from Google Fonts,
          which means your browser contacts a Google server and Google receives
          your IP address on every page — before any consent banner appears.
          Serving the font files from our own domain would remove this, and we
          intend to. Until then it is accurate to say that visiting this site
          tells Google you were here.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Two items of browser storage.</strong> Your answer to the consent
          banner is kept under <code>{ANALYTICS.consentKey}</code> so we do not ask
          again on every page, and the country you pick for pricing is kept under
          <code>suvi.country.v1</code>. Both stay in your browser and never leave
          your device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A guess at your country, made on your device.</strong> To show
          prices in your currency we read your browser's time zone and look the
          country up in a table built into the page. No request is made, nothing is
          sent to us or to anyone else, and we deliberately do not use an
          IP-location service — which would mean handing your address to a company
          that is not on the list below. The guess is often wrong for travellers
          and VPN users, so the price section carries a selector that overrides it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who else has your data</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Who</th><th>What they get</th><th>Why</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="https://getwaitlist.com/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">getwaitlist.com</a></td>
            <td>Email, page you signed up from, any answers you gave</td>
            <td>They run the waitlist</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Google Analytics</td>
            <td>Pages, approximate location, device — only after you accept</td>
            <td>To see what is worth writing more of</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Google Fonts</td>
            <td>Your IP address, on every page</td>
            <td>Typefaces. Being removed — see above</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>GitHub Pages</td>
            <td>Your IP address, in server logs</td>
            <td>Hosting</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        That is the complete list. We have never sold, rented or shared personal
        data with anyone else, and a business that needed to do so is not one we
        want to build.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Waitlist entries are kept until Suvi launches and you have had a
        reasonable chance to take up the invitation, or until you ask us to delete
        yours — whichever comes first. If the product never launches, we delete
        the list rather than keep it. Google Analytics data expires on Google's
        own retention schedule.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        If you are in the UK, the EEA, or anywhere with comparable law, you have
        the right to see what we hold about you, correct it, have it deleted, take
        it elsewhere, and object to our processing it. We extend the same
        treatment to everyone, wherever you live, because operating two standards
        would be more work than doing it properly once.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where we rely on consent — analytics — you can withdraw it at any time by
        clearing this site's data in your browser, which resets the banner.
        Where we rely on legitimate interest — holding your email so we can tell
        you the product exists — you can object, and we will delete the record.
      </p>
      <p>
        One email to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
        is enough. You do not need to cite a regulation or explain yourself, and
        we will confirm when it is done.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This website is written for parents and carers. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from anyone under 13, and there is nothing
        here for a child to sign up to.
      </p>
      <p>
        Suvi the product is intended for children, and that brings obligations we
        take seriously. Those obligations attach to the app, which does not exist
        yet. When it does, it will ship with its own policy covering what runs on
        a child's device, and we will publish that before anyone installs
        anything.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you believe a child has given us information through this site, email
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}> {SITE.contactEmail}</a> and we
        will remove it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        The date at the top is the last time this page changed. If we ever change
        it in a way that affects data we already hold, we will email the waitlist
        rather than quietly edit the page.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {AUTHOR.name}, {AUTHOR.role} —
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}> {SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
        A real person reads it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .pv { max-width: 720px; padding-block: clamp(36px, 6vw, 64px); }
  .pv__crumbs { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .pv__crumbs a { color: var(--muted); }
  .pv__crumbs a:hover { color: var(--brand); }
  .pv__h1 { font-size: clamp(30px, 5vw, 46px); letter-spacing: -1.2px; }
  .pv__meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .pv__body { margin-top: 34px; font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .pv__lede {
    font-size: 17.5px; padding: 18px 22px; margin-bottom: 12px;
    background: var(--brand-tint); border: 1px solid var(--brand-tint-border);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
  }
  .pv__body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 300; font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 28px);
    letter-spacing: -0.7px; color: var(--ink); margin-top: 42px; margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .pv__body h3 { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin-top: 26px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .pv__body p { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .pv__body ul { margin: 0 0 20px 22px; display: grid; gap: 9px; }
  .pv__body a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .pv__body code {
    font-size: 13.5px; background: var(--bg-warm);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-warm); border-radius: 5px; padding: 1px 6px;
  }
  .pv__body table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 22px; font-size: 14.5px; }
  .pv__body th, .pv__body td {
    text-align: left; padding: 10px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-warm);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .pv__body th { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.2px; color: var(--muted); }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .pv__body table, .pv__body thead, .pv__body tbody, .pv__body tr, .pv__body th, .pv__body td { display: block; }
    .pv__body thead { display: none; }
    .pv__body tr { padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-warm); }
    .pv__body td { border: 0; padding: 2px 0; }
  }
</style>
